## IMPLEMENTATION APPROACH

Based on the documentation provided from MDN Web Docs, implementing drag-and-drop file uploads and file API handling involves several core native browser APIs and event flows:

1. **HTML Drag and Drop API & Events**: 
   - To make an element a valid drop target, it must listen to and handle specific drag events: `dragenter`, `dragleave`, `dragover`, and `drop`.
   - **Preventing Default Browser Behavior**: By default, browsers may open or download dropped files. To prevent this, you must call `event.preventDefault()` and `event.stopPropagation()` on `dragenter`, `dragover`, and `drop` events. 
   - For file dropping specifically, browsers may also process files globally, so you often need to handle or cancel events appropriately. Note that `dragstart`, `drag,` and `dragend` do not fire when dragging files from the OS file explorer into the browser.

2. **DataTransfer & FileList**:
   - The `DragEvent` interface provides a `dataTransfer` property containing a `DataTransfer` object. 
   - Within the `drop` event handler, you can access the dropped files via `event.dataTransfer.files` (which returns a `FileList` of `File` objects) or through `event.dataTransfer.items` (using `DataTransferItemList` and `getAsFile()`).
   - Each `File` object contains useful metadata such as `name`, `size`, and `type` (MIME type).

3. **File API & FileReader**:
   - The `File API` allows web content to read the contents of local files selected via `<input type="file">` or via drag-and-drop.
   - The `FileReader` interface can be used asynchronously to read the contents of files (e.g., using `readAsDataURL()` for image previews or `readAsText()` for text documents).
   - Memory management: When generating object URLs or preview elements (like images), methods like `URL.createObjectURL()` and `URL.revokeObjectURL()` help manage resources effectively.

---

## WORKING EXAMPLE

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Drag and Drop File Upload Example</title>
    <style>
        #dropbox {
            width: 400px;
            height: 200px;
            border: 2px dashed #ccc;
            border-radius: 8px;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            text-align: center;
            font-family: sans-serif;
            color: #666;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        #dropbox.highlight {
            border-color: #000;
            background-color: #f9f9f9;
        }
        #preview {
            display: flex;
            gap: 10px;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
        }
        .preview-item {
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            padding: 5px;
            border-radius: 4px;
            text-align: center;
        }
        .preview-item img {
            max-width: 100px;
            max-height: 100px;
            display: block;
            margin-bottom: 5px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div id="dropbox">Drag and drop files here or use the input below</div>

    <input type="file" id="fileElem" multiple accept="image/*" style="display:none;">
    <label for="fileElem" style="cursor:pointer; display:inline-block; margin-bottom:20px; padding:6px 12px; background:#eee; border:1px solid #ccc; border-radius:4px; font-family:sans-serif;">Select some files</label>

    <div id="preview"></div>

    <script>
        const dropbox = document.getElementById("dropbox");
        const fileElem = document.getElementById("fileElem");
        const preview = document.getElementById("preview");

        // Prevent default drag behaviors on the window/document if necessary
        ;['dragenter', 'dragover', 'dragleave', 'drop'].forEach(eventName => {
            window.addEventListener(eventName, preventDefaults, false);
            dropbox.addEventListener(eventName, preventDefaults, false);
        });

        function preventDefaults(e) {
            e.preventDefault();
            e.stopPropagation();
        }

        // Highlight drop zone when item is dragged over it
        ;['dragenter', 'dragover'].forEach(eventName => {
            dropbox.addEventListener(eventName, () => dropbox.classList.add('highlight'), false);
        });

        ;['dragleave', 'drop'].forEach(eventName => {
            dropbox.addEventListener(eventName, () => dropbox.classList.remove('highlight'), false);
        });

        // Handle dropped files
        dropbox.addEventListener('drop', handleDrop, false);

        // Handle selected files from input element
        fileElem.addEventListener('change', function(e) {
            handleFiles(this.files);
        }, false);

        function handleDrop(e) {
            const dt = e.dataTransfer;
            const files = dt.files;
            handleFiles(files);
        }

        function handleFiles(files) {
            files = [...files];
            files.forEach(uploadFile);
        }

        function uploadFile(file) {
            // Display file info and preview using FileReader / Object URL
            const itemDiv = document.createElement('div');
            itemDiv.className = 'preview-item';

            if (file.type.startsWith('image/')) {
                const img = document.createElement('img');
                img.src = URL.createObjectURL(file);
                img.onload = () => {
                    // Clean up memory once loaded
                    URL.revokeObjectURL(img.src);
                }
                itemDiv.appendChild(img);
            }

            const info = document.createElement('p');
            info.textContent = `${file.name} (${Math.round(file.size / 1024)} KB)`;
            info.style.fontSize = "12px";
            itemDiv.appendChild(info);

            preview.appendChild(itemDiv);
        }
    </script>

</body>
</html>
```
